----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party sources in this repository (the BSD 3-Clause licence above is
unchanged and covers the original work of this project only)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains reference material from third parties.  The notes
below state what is known; they are not legal advice and make no claim beyond
that.  Files under original/ are kept unchanged for research and comparison.

* original/unix-v7/ -- UNIX Version 7 (Bell Laboratories, 1979), as distributed
  in Henry Spencer's tarball from the Unix Heritage Society (TUHS).  Released
  in 2002 under the Caldera licence (BSD-style):
  https://www.tuhs.org/Archive/Caldera-license.pdf

* original/sys3/ -- UNIX System III (PDP-11 and VAX), from the GitHub mirror
  Krush206/unix-system-III.  The 2002 Caldera licence does not mention System
  III explicitly.  The files are included for research purposes on the
  decision of the project owner; the authenticity of the mirror has not been
  checked against a TUHS original.

* original/hippe-v7/ -- the collection "Torsten_Hippe_v7" from the TUHS
  archive (Distributions/Research), assembled in 1995 from sources unknown to
  us; the person who assembled the collection is not the author of its contents.  Its
  UNIX V7 base falls under the Caldera licence.  For additions by third
  parties no licence statement is known, and their authors are unknown.  The
  files are included for research and comparison purposes on the decision of
  the project owner.

* original/wega/ -- contains only a reference note (README); no WEGA source is
  copied into this repository.

* Reconstructed MUTOS sources (kernel/, mutos_io/, userspace/) -- MUTOS 8000
  is a derivative of UNIX Version 7.  The reconstructed sources are the
  result of research on the original binaries; where they follow V7 text (or
  the text of the collection above), that text remains subject to the terms
  stated for its source.  The original MUTOS disk images under disks/original/
  are kept for research.
